	(text_box "1. Function: Passive 6-layer pass-through router connecting the upper 4-ASIC stack (J3, top DF40C-80DP) 1:1 to drive-board socket J5 (bottom DF40C-80DS). R6 (10k to AGND_J5) holds the analog ASIC_AC_IN input of all eight ASICs at 0 V default, and TP7 provides a top-side SE-corner probe/injection pad reachable with all four ASIC boards fitted. The eight south-row rails (DVDD, VDD10, VDD_DRIVER, REF_VCM, VDD_FE, REF_VDD, VSS10, VDD_ADC) and AGND remain split per port (_J5 / _J6) on the router and are tied together on both drive boards (Option B LDO Board V3 and 4K Direct Carrier V7).\n\n2. Source / changes: Designed by Antigravity from Option B Router V3 contract review (24 Nov 2026: PIN_MAP_B_V2.csv, ASIC_PORT_PINS_V8.csv, SYNTHESIS.md sections 3-4, D1_straight_minimal/DESIGN.md, HANDOFF_ROUTING_V1.md) and Router V2 (FPGA_LDO_B_Router_Layout_V2). Hirose DF40 series data sheets as filed by LCSC: C294544 DF40C-80DP-0.4V(51) https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C294544.pdf (5759 orderable, read 2026-11-25 07:26 CST) and C312960 DF40C-80DS-0.4V(51) https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C312960.pdf (5266 orderable, read 2026-11-25 07:26 CST); R6 Uniroyal 0402WGF1002TCE JLC Basic C25744 https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C25744.pdf (27098412 orderable, read 2026-11-25 07:26 CST). Changes from Router V2: single 120-pin J5 replaced by 2 x DF40C-80DS (J5, J6); port pins 3/5 grounded (Pin Map V7); separate BOARD3_SPI_LATCH on J3.61/J5.61 (Pin Map V8); port capacitors C51/C53-C57 removed and moved to the drive boards (17 x 1 uF C52923 each); R6/TP7 kept on router and moved to top SE corner; In3 plane changed from AGND to GND so all four signal layers reference continuous GND planes. Unverified: DF40 30-cycle mating wear (consumable vs saver board) and JLC HDI via-in-pad review."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.42 360.68 0)
		(size 340 25.6)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.35 1.35)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d9b14cea-3468-5040-8fdf-d3ee643595cb")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: Connects the lower 4-ASIC stack (J4, bottom DF40C-80DS) to drive-board socket J6 (bottom DF40C-80DS) with odd/even pin pairs swapped (J6 pin 2k+1 = J4 pin 2k+2, J6 pin 2k+2 = J4 pin 2k+1) so every signal lane runs straight north-south with zero crossovers. ASIC_VDD_CGEN (J3.1/J4.1/J5.1/J6.2), ASIC_AC_IN (J3.69/J4.69/J5.69/J6.70), the seven *_SHARED controls (STIM_EN/START/CHB/CLK, FE_RESET, IMP_TST, CHIP_RESET), and GND (In2/In3 planes, pins 3/5/46/48 on J3/J4/J5 and 4/6/45/47 on J6) are tied across both ports on the router.\n\n2. Source / changes: Designed by Antigravity from PIN_MAP_B_V2.csv (J6 odd/even swap approved by Howard 24 Nov 2026; Frontend contract PIN_MAP_V8 unchanged) and SYNTHESIS.md sections 3-4. Same Hirose DF40C-80DS-0.4V(51) C312960 sockets cited in the J3/J5 block. Mechanical envelope: 22.69 x 17.62 mm rectangle (x 88.655-111.345, y 110.315-127.935, south edge <= 127.96 mm for 0.525 mm clearance to Frontend V14 / XEM8305); lower-ASIC side-pin bottom keep-out x 88.7-91.5, y 115.2-117.3; J6 at (99.783, 120.200) and J5 at (99.783, 125.200), 5.00 mm pitch. Copper plan choice open for Howard before routing: D1 straight-lane + D3 ground corridor (recommended; 1+4+1 laser+buried in-pad) vs D3 (no via-in-pad, lowest fab risk). Unverified: JLC HDI approval and impedance stack."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 441.96 360.68 0)
		(size 340 21.5)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
